fact WorkItem(id: "WI-962", description: some(value: "SCALAND: `UnresolvedName.scopeName` IS FILLED THREE WAYS, AND ONE OF THEM IS THE LITERAL STRING \"requires\". The field renders as `unresolved name 'x' in scope '<scopeName>'`, so it is a claim about WHICH SCOPE WAS SEARCHED. Its call sites disagree about what it means. (1) `Loader.load`'s pending-import retry passes `p.scopeName` = the IMPORTED PATH (`PendingImport.scopeName`) — a different but defensible meaning, 'the scope searched INTO'. (2) `processRequires` hardcodes `\"requires\"`, which names no scope at all: the reader is told the error happened 'in scope requires'. It is the WRONG one, and cheaply so — `processRequires` ALREADY has `scopeTerm: TermId` in hand, which is exactly what WI-957's `Loader.scopeDisplayName` turns into a real qualified name (`demo.C`). (3) WI-957's own `AmbiguousSymbol` reads it off `scopeTerm` via that helper. WORK: give the requires site the real scope name, and decide whether the pending-import meaning stays distinct (if so, SAY so at the field, because two meanings on one field with no note is how (2) got written). WHILE THERE: `scopeDisplayName` is currently `Loader`-private with ONE caller, which is why WI-957 left it there — a second caller is what justifies promoting it next to `KnowledgeBase.qualifiedNameOf`, so that 'what do we call this scope in a diagnostic' has ONE answer rather than a helper each. `isSortScope` already open-codes the same 'unwrap a scope term to its nullary Fn functor' step, making it a third instance of the unwrap. ACCEPTANCE: the existing `DiagnosticLocationTest` case 'an unresolved name is located at the name' asserts only the SPAN today — extend it (or add a sibling) to assert the scope NAME is the enclosing sort's qualified name, and say at the site which test fails when the change is backed out. NOTE this is pre-existing — WI-957 did not introduce it, it made the fix available. Related: WI-961."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "scaland-sbt-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-08-04T05:10:27Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-962", name: "scaland")
